.TH ESL 1 "March 2026" "ecoSignalLab 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
esl \- ecoSignalLab command-line acoustic analysis toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esl
.RI [ global-options ] " command " [ command-options ]
.br
.B esl
.B quickstart
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBesl\fR is a CLI-first toolkit for environmental and architectural acoustics.
It supports multi-channel analysis, calibration-aware metrics, novelty detection,
batch processing, and machine-learning exports.
.SH PRIMARY COMMANDS
.TP
\fBesl doctor\fR
Check environment readiness, decode dependencies, and optional input-file metadata.
.TP
\fBesl simple\fR
Print a compact human-readable summary for one file.
.TP
\fBesl analyze\fR
Analyze one audio file and export JSON/CSV/Parquet/HDF5/MAT + plots.
.TP
\fBesl batch\fR
Analyze a directory of files with optional recursive scan and report metrics.
.TP
\fBesl moments extract\fR
Find interesting moments and export clips plus timestamped CSV/JSON reports.
.TP
\fBesl similar\fR
Find the N most similar files in a corpus relative to a query file.
.TP
\fBesl stream\fR
Run chunked streaming-style analysis with threshold rules and alert traces.
.TP
\fBesl calibrate check\fR
Run calibration drift checks from tone captures.
.TP
\fBesl schema\fR
Print or export the active JSON output schema.
.TP
\fBesl docs\fR
Build documentation in HTML/PDF.
.SH GLOBAL CLI BEHAVIOR
.TP
\fB\-\-verbosity 0..3\fR
0=silent, 1=summary, 2=detailed, 3=full diagnostic.
.TP
\fB\-\-debug 0..2\fR
0=none, 1=processing details, 2=internal traces.
.TP
\fB\-\-device auto|cpu|cuda|mps\fR
Select compute backend for tensor and ML-adjacent paths.
.SH CALIBRATION FIELDS
Calibration YAML/JSON may define:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdbfs_reference\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBspl_reference_db\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBweighting\fR (A/C/Z)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmic_sensitivity_mv_pa\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpreamp_gain_db\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBadc_full_scale_vrms\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcalibration_tone_file\fR
.PP
Precision pressure conversion (\fBPa <-> dBFS\fR) is available when
\fBmic_sensitivity_mv_pa\fR, \fBpreamp_gain_db\fR, and
\fBadc_full_scale_vrms\fR are all provided.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check environment + input readiness:
.B esl doctor input.wav
.TP
Print a short summary:
.B esl simple input.wav
.TP
Analyze one file:
.B esl analyze input.wav --out-dir out --json out/input.json --plot
.TP
Extract one top-ranked moment:
.B esl moments extract input.wav --out out/moments --single --rank-metric novelty_curve --event-window 8
.TP
Run similarity search:
.B esl similar query.wav corpus_dir --top-k 10 --json out/similarity.json
.TP
Run calibration drift check with pressure chain:
.B esl calibrate check --tone calib.wav --calibration examples/calibration.yaml --preamp-gain-db 34 --adc-full-scale-vrms 1.0
.SH FILES
.TP
